{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>daughter of Anah, daughter of Zibeon.</b> Now we find that there is Anah the brother of Zibeon, and also the name of his son is Anah. Therefore one may say that the father and the son, or the two brothers, lay with one woman, and those born were not known whose sons they were. It is possible that this is Oholibamah daughter of Anah who is the son of Zibeon, and Scripture attributes her to the name of her father and her father's father, to distinguish between Anah and Anah. Some say there is Korah son of Adah and there is Korah son of Oholibamah. What seems close to me is that he is the son of Oholibamah, and he is one person, and Scripture mentions him among the chieftains of Eliphaz because he dwelt with them. It is also possible that his mother died, for he is the youngest of Oholibamah's sons, and Adah raised Korah with her sons, and it was written of him that he is among her sons, like the sons of Michal, and she had no son. And so Amalek was written among the sons of Adah because he was the son of her husband's maidservant." "He explains: אלוף [alluf] means chieftain and great one, and it is not like ככבש אלוף (Jeremiah 11:19); rather the כ [kaf] serves for itself [i.e., as a comparative] and that which follows along with it. Thus it is: ככבש כאלוף [like a lamb, like a companion], for so is the way of the sacred language to speak thus, like כריע כאח לי [like a brother to me]. The translator [Targum] rendered: גבורים [mighty ones] (Psalms 35:14):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The closing comparison 'like the sons of Michal' alludes to 2 Samuel 21:8, where Michal's sons are actually her sister Merab's; Ibn Ezra's syntax is compressed here and I have preserved the compression."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:12.660047813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}